From 18456419e45c198c7b07d5b7b6ef57b03017af54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T <t@d.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:58:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Item 8 correction: a real matched null replaces the rank. The
 previous implementation fed pricing_columns the family's OWN VALID rows and
 its OWN pass rate, so pf_null_exceedance_pct was a within-family rank,
 EXPECTED_ROWS_AT_OR_ABOVE_THIS_PF was the count of rows at or above that PF,
 and expected_valid_by_chance_family reduced to len(VALID) - tautological, and
 identical for a family of pure noise and a family of genuine edge.
 draw_matched_null_masks now generates K signals per family from the same
 post-hygiene vocabulary as random 1-3 condition conjunctions, accepted only
 when the fire count lands within tolerance of a target sampled from that
 family's own fire-count distribution, seeded and recorded; they are scored
 through the identical path and run through the identical VALID predicate by
 matched_null_rate, which was previously defined and called nowhere.
 null_quality blanks the Appendix A names with a stated reason rather than
 emitting a confident number when K is too small, and the catalogue header
 only claims to price the operator's search when a real null priced it. Item
 5's in-run half added: assert_episode_thresholds_mechanism_d byte-verifies
 the four market-object modules against Appendix D's constants and aborts if
 the episode K/E arrays are scalars rather than per-bar oracle output. Item
 6's n_valid_triples_touching is BLANK when no F0 rows exist, never 0.

---
 dot_master_discovery/engine/catalogue.py | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 dot_master_discovery/master.py           |  88 +++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 198 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

